HyperFrames — https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The audio plugin adopts ideas
from HyperFrames' hyperframes-audio and media-use skills (voiceover carve with
sidechain ducking, a separate music stem, and the audio_meta.json hand-off
shape). No HyperFrames text or code is copied; where a guide paraphrases an
idea, docs/coverage/audio-sources.md says so.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled nonverbal clips and example sounds
plugins/audio/tools/assets/nonverbal contains CC0 1.0 recordings from
Freesound (via Openverse); every file's source, creator and license check is
listed in its CREDITS.json. The example renders use further CC0 and CC BY
sounds, each credited in that example's CREDITS.md. The audiobook example
reads a public-domain text (Arthur Conan Doyle, "A Study in Scarlet", 1887,
via Project Gutenberg).
